Author: Nathan Krupa <54715560+NathanKrupa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Jun 19 13:50:30 2026 -0400

    security(SEC-006): inline SSRF guard at the direct httpx sinks (#1429)
    
    Replace the helper-based first cut with the simpler inline pattern that
    the boy-scout file-scoped ratchet accepts: fetch the URL the validator
    returned, ``httpx.get(validate_http_url(url))``, at each existing sink.
    
    - safe_http stays pure (no httpx call → no SVC-006 in the file-scoped
      ratchet run); validate_http_url just gains a ``-> str`` return.
    - cli/gov.py and services/pdf_extractor.py inline the guard at the sink;
      SEC-006 noqa removed, STAB-008 noqa kept (degradation is the caller's).
    - Boy-scout: extract a _dollars() helper in gov.py's program-table echo
      to remove the 3x ``${...:>14,}`` duplication (8 -> 7 findings); fold the
      safe_http reject tests so the parametrized-url pass-through CPLX-002
      clears (1 -> 0).
    - Tests assert blocked URLs (private/link-local/loopback IP, non-http
      scheme) raise before the sink, and that the validator returns the URL.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

